[00:00.34]Lesson 21 | 第21课
[00:02.21]Daniel Mendoza | 丹尼尔·门多萨
[00:09.93]How many unsuccessful attempts did Mendoza make before becoming Champion of all England? | 门多萨成为全英冠军之前失败过多少次？
[00:18.59]Boxing matches were very popular in England two hundred years ago. | 两百年前，拳击比赛在英国非常盛行。
[00:23.52]In those days, boxers fought with bare fists for prize money. | 那时，拳击家们赤手空拳进行角逐以获取奖金。
[00:28.93]Because of this, they were known as 'prizefighters'. | 因此，他们被称作“职业拳击手”。
[00:33.27]However, boxing was very crude, | 不过，拳击十分粗野，
[00:36.63]for there were no rules and a prizefighter could be seriously injured or even killed during a match. | 因为没有规则，职业拳击手可能在比赛中受重伤，甚至丧命。
[00:44.94]One of the most colourful figures in boxing history was Daniel Mendoza, who was born in 1764. | 拳击史上最引人注目的人物之一是丹尼尔·门多萨，他生于1764年。
[00:53.56]The use of gloves was not introduced until 1860, when the Marquis of Queensberry drew up the first set of rules. | 直到1860年昆斯伯里侯爵制定出第一套规则，手套才被采用。
[01:02.63]Though he was technically a prizefighter, | 虽然门多萨严格来说只是个职业拳击手，
[01:05.75]Mendoza did much to change crude prizefighting into a sport, for he brought science to the game. | 但他为把粗野的拳击变成一项体育运动做了很多贡献，是他把科学引入了这项运动。
[01:13.71]In his day, Mendoza enjoyed tremendous popularity. | 门多萨在的全盛时期深受大家欢迎。
[01:18.41]He was adored by rich and poor alike. | 无论是富人还是穷人都对他崇拜备至。
[01:21.94]Mendoza rose to fame swiftly after a boxing match when he was only fourteen years old. | 门多萨14岁时参加了一场拳击赛，之后迅速成名。
[01:28.42]This attracted the attention of Richard Humphries who was then the most eminent boxer in England. | 这引起了当时英国最杰出的拳击家理查德·汉弗莱斯的注意。
[01:35.87]He offered to train Mendoza and his young pupil was quick to learn. | 他提出训练门多萨，而这个年轻学生一学就会。
[01:40.98]In fact, Mendoza soon became so successful that Humphries turned against him. | 事实上，门多萨不久便非常成功，汉弗莱斯反而与他反目成仇。
[01:48.01]The two men quarrelled bitterly and it was clear that the argument could only be settled by a fight. | 两人激烈争吵了一番，显然，这场争端只能通过打斗来解决。
[01:56.50]A match was held at Stilton, where both men fought for an hour. | 于是在斯蒂尔顿进行了一场比赛，两人打了一个小时。
[02:01.60]The public bet a great deal of money on Mendoza, but he was defeated. | 公众把大笔赌注押在门多萨身上，可他却被打败了。
[02:07.22]Mendoza met Humphries in the ring on a later occasion and he lost for a second time. | 后来门多萨与汉弗莱斯又在拳台上较量，他第二次又输了。
[02:13.97]It was not until his third match in 1790 that he finally beat Humphries and became Champion of England. | 直到1790年第三次比赛，他才终于击败汉弗莱斯，成为全英拳击冠军。
[02:23.50]Meanwhile, he founded a highly successful Academy and even Lord Byron became one of his pupils. | 与此同时，他创办了一所极为成功的拳击学校，连拜伦勋爵也成了他的学生。
[02:31.59]He earned enormous sums of money and was paid as much as ￡100 for a single appearance. | 他挣了大笔的钱，一次出场便可获得多达100英镑的报酬。
[02:39.85]Despite this, he was so extravagant that he was always in debt. | 尽管如此，他挥霍无度，总是债台高筑。
[02:45.91]After he was defeated by a boxer called Gentleman Jackson, he was quickly forgotten. | 他被一位人称“绅士杰克”的拳击手击败后，很快被人遗忘了。
[02:52.53]He was sent to prison for failing to pay his debts and died in poverty in 1836. | 他因无力还债而被捕入狱，1836年在贫困中死去。
